WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:02.368
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.402
I'm so happy you came back.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.603
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.272
-I want to come back
one more time.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.273
-You do?
-Yeah.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.441
-Okay.
-In a little while.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.609
-Really?
-Yes.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.810
-You'll just surprise me?
-Yup.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.278
-Can we talk about
your album, by the way?

00:00:12.344 --> 00:00:14.246
Number one holiday album
right here, "Christmas."

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:15.981
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:18.617
Number one, doesn't get
bigger than number one.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:20.019
-No.
-Congratulations.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.487
-Thank you.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.689
-Why is it taking so long
to put out a holiday album?

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.626
-Because I could --
Oh, because I couldn't --

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.530
This sounds so stupid.
I couldn't find myself in a --

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.899
I couldn't see myself
in a Christmas album.

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.534
And so I just said
to the record company

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:39.805
if you just leave me alone,
and...

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.807
Right,
and I -- and I was in my house.

00:00:41.874 --> 00:00:43.243
I recorded most of it
in my house,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.878
some of it in England
with my producer.

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:49.249
But I just picked out
these kind of songs

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.250
that don't necessarily
go together.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.652
But when you put them together,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:54.420
they're really good
and they're all --

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.855
It's just to have
a happy thing.

00:00:55.921 --> 00:00:58.791
Chuck Berry, and Stevie sings
on the album with me.

00:00:58.857 --> 00:00:59.993
He sings on the song.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.327
-How did you get?
How did you get --

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:02.695
I mean, obviously you're Cher,
you just called.

00:01:02.761 --> 00:01:04.096
But how did you get
Stevie Wonder to go

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:05.598
yeah, I'll do, what,
Christmas -- he'll do.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.333
-No, I was so terrified.
I'm not kidding.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.467
I was.
-You?

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:12.004
-I'm not kidding.
I was like, ooh.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:15.475
I called him because, look,
I'd done the song,

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:19.545
but there was just some parts
of it that were just Stevie.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.715
I couldn't find it
and it was just Stevie.

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:27.987
So I called him and -- and I
said, "Hi, Stevie, it's me.

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:31.724
And he said, hi,
and how are you?

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.427
And I was like, into it.
Well, see, this is what I want.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:37.897
I know how are you,
but I just said

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:40.199
I've done your song and I --

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:43.102
but there are some parts
I can't do, I just can't do it.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.904
And he said, "Okay,
consider it done."

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:49.242
It was like, well, "Do you not
want me to pitch it more?"

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:51.076
-He just said yes immediately.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.745
-And he was like, yeah,
I'll just redo the parts,

00:01:52.811 --> 00:01:54.147
whatever parts you want
me to do.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:55.748
-He didn't even know
what I wanted him to do.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.516
I just said,
I'll send it to you.

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.518
And so -- and he did it.
It's so good.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:01.520
Alright,
but that's not the cool part.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:05.825
So at the end, in the middle
he says, is it my song?

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.427
And I went, well, yeah,
it's your song.

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:09.628
And then at the end
he said, "Hey,

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:10.864
Cher, Cher, Cher."
And I went, "What?"

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.801
He said, "Do you want me
to play harmonica?"

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.135
-Now the gift just keeps giving.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.037
And you go, oh, my gosh.
Did you start crying?

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:20.506
-And the truth is no matter
what kind of mood I'm in,

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.709
when I hear him play
the harmonica, I can only smile.

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.878
But that's not the best part.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.047
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:31.651
So when I hung up, I ran around
my room, jumped on my bed.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.586
I jumped up and down
and just kept screaming.

00:02:33.652 --> 00:02:35.555
Stevie Wonder is going to be
on my album.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.056
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.057
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:41.493
-Just like a little kid.
-Yeah.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:44.464
-It's phenomenal. There's so
many good jams on here.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.032
"DJ Play a Christmas Song,"
by the way,

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:47.600
that's my jam.
I love that one.

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:49.702
That's my fave on this one.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.638
Ooh, ooh, look at this.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.840
Well, I mean, come on.
You thought of everything.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:58.811
-No, but with Tyga,
and that's really cool.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.312
-Tyga's a great one, too.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:02.548
And, um, oh, Darlene Love.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:03.949
-Darlene Love.
Wait.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.486
I have a little trivia
about this that I did not know.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:09.655
This is -- So "Christmas
(Baby Please Come Home)."

00:03:09.721 --> 00:03:11.658
♪ Christmas snow's coming down ♪

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.092
Right? So you do that
with Darlene Love.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.527
You go that makes sense.
Great.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:16.962
Turns out you sang backup
on the original.

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:19.131
-When I was 17.
-What?

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:20.933
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.670
I never -- I never knew that.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.638
What was that like?
I mean, that's well.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.573
-I got the -- I got the gig.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.076
Well, Sonny had told
Phillip Spector

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.412
Cher sings, and he was like,
yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:37.382
But then one night Darlene's
car broke down and he said,

00:03:37.449 --> 00:03:38.685
Sonny said, do you sing?

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.119
And while I'm trying to qualify,

00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:42.187
he said, I just need to know
he's get out there.

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:46.125
So I went out
and I was terrified

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:49.028
because Phillip was asking
everybody what's your part.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.763
And I was thinking
I don't know my part.

00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:53.165
And I just singing,
I'm copying somebody.

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.601
And that was -- I did it.
He never did --

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.537
He never worked
without me again

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:00.706
until the last song I did was
"You Lost That Loving Feeling."

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.275
-Wow.
I have a picture of you.

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:05.644
This is you and Darlene Love
from that session.

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.413
How cool is that?

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:10.483
And now she's singing
on your album.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.017
It's full circle.
-Yeah, it is.

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:13.686
It's kind of fantastic.

00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:16.155
When you're in New York,
you never call me or ask

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.190
if you want to hang out or...

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:21.059
And I just think
that's kind of interesting.

00:04:21.126 --> 00:04:23.262
What do you like to do?
What does Cher do in New York?

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:26.833
I read somewhere that
you love Serendipity 3.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:28.000
-Yeah.
-Yeah, I've been

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.436
going there since I was 19.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.837
-This place,
Serendipity 3,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.005
and you get
the frozen hot chocolate.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:34.473
Yeah.
-Anyways, it's one of my

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.276
favorite spots, but you can't
get in in the city.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:37.643
Obviously you can get in.
-I can get in.

00:04:37.709 --> 00:04:39.077
-You're Cher.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:40.579
Yeah, you can go in there.

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:43.082
-No, but I've known them
since I was 19 years old.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:45.317
I can get in
because I've got seniority.

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:46.585
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:49.521
-You got -- you got.
-You have great teeth.

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:51.390
-I do?
-Yeah.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.127
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:57.930
-But now you're
a little bit red.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:01.701
-Yeah. No, yeah.
You have the Christmas album.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:05.471
You have "Believe,"
the deluxe edition.

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.872
Look at this.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:09.975
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.243
This is. Yeah.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.778
-And then I --

00:05:12.844 --> 00:05:15.214
-I feel like we're at
the Home Shopping Network.

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:18.751
-We're getting to the blenders.
When only have five left.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.420
But you you're coming out
with your memoir.

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:23.455
-Yeah.
-And I want -- This is exciting.

00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:24.857
-Ugh.
-No. What do you mean?

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.025
You know why?

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:28.094
Because I just
totally chickened out,

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.529
because I was --

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.898
I guess I was -- I don't know
what I was.

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.599
I just was totally
chickening out,

00:05:33.665 --> 00:05:38.437
but I -- I didn't put in
some things that need to be in,

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:41.607
and they're not comfortable,
but they need to be in.

00:05:41.673 --> 00:05:44.477
So I have to go
back and man up.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:46.111
-You got to do it.
-Yeah.

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:47.546
-It's like it's
beyond therapy.

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:48.981
It's tough.
-Yeah.

00:05:49.047 --> 00:05:51.484
-And also I've lived
too long and done too much.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:54.353
And so it's like
it should be the encyclopedia,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.123
not that you guys know
what that is.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.024
-Do you have a title for it?

00:05:59.091 --> 00:06:00.559
-No.

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:02.595
-Should we come up with one?

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.262
[ Audience shouting ]

00:06:04.329 --> 00:06:05.430
-Oh.

00:06:05.497 --> 00:06:07.266
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:08.701
That could be.
a great game.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:10.602
-Yeah, yeah.
How about --

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:14.240
Alright, wait, so how about...
Alright.

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:15.775
So you're going to -- you're
going to -- you're going to tell

00:06:15.841 --> 00:06:17.843
some things that
you probably shouldn't tell.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.612
-Yeah.
-Maybe "I Got Scoops, Babe."

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:22.614
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:23.949
Alright, that got groans.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:27.319
-I'm totally set up
for this one, right?

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.355
I'm really tired from surfing
in the audience, okay?

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:32.024
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.193
-That was amazing, by the way.
That was amazing what you did.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.729
That was dangerous.
Please don't ever do that again.

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:40.032
-I'm not, and I'm old. I can't
be doing that kind of [bleep].

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:45.771
-Well, I can't wait
to read the book,

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:48.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I'm just going
to say right now, yes.

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.142
-What do you mean?

00:06:50.208 --> 00:06:51.944
-You're going to ask me
if you want my permission

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.880
should I be in your book,
and yes.

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:57.416
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:59.585
If it's -- it's a big book.

00:06:59.651 --> 00:07:01.620
If it's a big book, come on.

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:05.958
This Cher already said yes.
This Cher said yes.

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:07.459
This Cher already said yes,
I'm in the book.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:08.760
Am I in the book.

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:11.430
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:12.965
-Yeah.
-Oh, how about this one?

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:14.366
-That Cher's pliable, okay?

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:15.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:19.004
-Maybe Over Chering.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:21.406
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:21.473 --> 00:07:26.045 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:26.111 --> 00:07:28.247
I'm telling you.

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:30.148
I love you.
I always love seeing you.

00:07:30.215 --> 00:07:32.952
I love having you on.
Congrats on the Christmas album.

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:35.721
I thought that we could maybe
do a little fun celebration

00:07:35.787 --> 00:07:37.289
for -- for this album.

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:42.061
So I actually talked to the
people over at "Serendipity 3"

00:07:42.127 --> 00:07:44.597
and had them make us
a frozen hot chocolate.

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:46.665
-Ooh.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:51.637
-This is ice cold
from Serendipity 3.

00:07:51.703 --> 00:07:53.271
Should we have a sip and cheers?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:54.940
Cheers.-

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:58.643
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.013
-It's really cold.
Really good.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.216
That is Cher
right there, everybody.

